\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Naive validation versus the audit, against pressure outcomes (math; the ten in-domain-audited judge configurations plus the trained reward model).} Gap = excess hack gap at best-of-64: how much the judge's own scores inflate relative to true quality, in baseline standard deviations over a permutation null. Regret = accuracy left on the table versus best-possible selection. Bootstrap 95\% CIs in brackets. The 1.5B-blind bootstrap resamples are degenerate (concentrated scores), so its conviction carries jackknife and permutation inference instead: style partial $+0.51$, jackknife CI $[+0.13, +0.89]$, permutation $p = 0.0017$ (two-sided, $n{=}53$). Per-configuration excess-gap CIs for all twelve math configurations are in \texttt  {papers/analysis/gap\_cis.json}. Under the frozen verdict rule the 14B-blind row is a false pass (Section~\ref {sec:pressure}). \textbf  {Takeaway: raw agreement conflates the sabotaged frontier judge ($+0.35$) with the honest blind 14B ($+0.37$) although their pressure behavior differs in kind; the style partial separates them ($+0.59$ vs.\ $-0.21$) and identifies the failure mode.}}}{5}{table.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:h2h}{{1}{5}{\textbf {Naive validation versus the audit, against pressure outcomes (math; the ten in-domain-audited judge configurations plus the trained reward model).} Gap = excess hack gap at best-of-64: how much the judge's own scores inflate relative to true quality, in baseline standard deviations over a permutation null. Regret = accuracy left on the table versus best-possible selection. Bootstrap 95\% CIs in brackets. The 1.5B-blind bootstrap resamples are degenerate (concentrated scores), so its conviction carries jackknife and permutation inference instead: style partial $+0.51$, jackknife CI $[+0.13, +0.89]$, permutation $p = 0.0017$ (two-sided, $n{=}53$). Per-configuration excess-gap CIs for all twelve math configurations are in \texttt {papers/analysis/gap\_cis.json}. Under the frozen verdict rule the 14B-blind row is a false pass (Section~\ref {sec:pressure}). \textbf {Takeaway: raw agreement conflates the sabotaged frontier judge ($+0.35$) with the honest blind 14B ($+0.37$) although their pressure behavior differs in kind; the style partial separates them ($+0.59$ vs.\ $-0.21$) and identifies the failure mode.}}{table.caption.8}{}}
